        "statement": "Let two finite based knot diagrams be joined along their marked arcs in a planar pointed connected-sum diagram, without new crossings. The odd complexes admit a normalized bigraded right $\\mathbb A=\\mathbb Z[X]/(X^2)$-linear chain isomorphism\n$$ C_o(D_1)\\otimes_{\\mathbb A}C_o(D_2)\\{-1\\}\\ \\cong\\ C_o(D_1\\#D_2), $$\nand the Bar–Natan complexes admit the corresponding marked $\\mathbb R=\\mathbb Z[h,X]/(X^2-hX)$-linear chain isomorphism. In the odd case the induced signs realize the full prescribed face products, so admissible sign comparison applies, including zero-composite faces. The two isomorphisms agree after reduction modulo $2$ and $(2,h)$ under the statewise comparison. Their construction is finite and choice-free.",
